  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 17 files needed for this analysis, covering both sides of the dependency chain:\n\n**Spring Boot detection/auto-config side:**\n- `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java` \u2014 the `Factory` inner class detects Log4j2 by checking for `org.apache.logging.log4j.core.impl.Log4jContextFactory` on the classpath (not log4j-api or log4j-to-slf4j directly)\n- `LoggingSystem.java`, `LoggingSystemFactory.java`, `spring.factories` \u2014 the SPI mechanism that orders Logback > Log4j2 > JUL\n- `LogbackLoggingSystem.java` \u2014 comparison case (detects via `ch.qos.logback.classic.LoggerContext`)\n- `AbstractLoggingSystem.java`, `LoggingApplicationListener.java` \u2014 the initialization pipeline that invokes the detection\n- `spring-boot-dependencies/build.gradle` \u2014 pins Log4j2 to 2.20.0 via `log4j-bom`, SLF4J to 2.0.7, Logback to 1.4.7\n\n**Log4j2 bridge module side:**\n- `log4j-to-slf4j/pom.xml`, `SLF4JProvider.java`, `SLF4JLoggerContextFactory.java`, `META-INF/services/org.apache.logging.log4j.spi.Provider` \u2014 the log4j-api\u2192SLF4J bridge, registered via the modern `ServiceLoader`-based `Provider` SPI (compatible version `\"2.6.0\"`)\n- `log4j-api/spi/Provider.java`, `util/ProviderUtil.java` \u2014 the Provider abstraction itself, which supports both the legacy `META-INF/log4j-provider.properties` mechanism and the newer `ServiceLoader` mechanism\n- `log4j-core/impl/Log4jContextFactory.java` \u2014 the class Spring Boot's classpath check actually looks for\n- `log4j-api/pom.xml`, root `pom.xml` \u2014 module/version context\n\nKey finding embedded in these files: Spring Boot's `Log4J2LoggingSystem.Factory` never references `log4j-to-slf4j` or `log4j-api` symbols directly \u2014 detection hinges entirely on `log4j-core`'s `Log4jContextFactory`. `log4j-to-slf4j` and `log4j-core` are mutually exclusive on the classpath (enforced at runtime in `SLF4JLoggerContextFactory`'s constructor), so which bridge module is present determines whether Spring Boot activates `Log4J2LoggingSystem` or falls through to `LogbackLoggingSystem`.",
